cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived data, please cite the archived release and the two source studies below."
title: "phosphosite-proximity: code and derived data for distance-to-annotated-residue features in yeast and human phosphosite-mutant screens"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Kyle
    affiliation: "Human Biology, College of Natural Sciences, The University of Texas at Austin"
  - family-names: Marchenko
    given-names: Arkady
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, College of Natural Sciences, The University of Texas at Austin"
  - family-names: Chang
    given-names: David
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Cockrell School of Engineering, The University of Texas at Austin"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kyle-nguyen-git/phosphosite-proximity"
abstract: >-
  Code, derived cohorts and the numerical authority for an audit of the distance from a
  phosphosite to the nearest UniProt-annotated active or binding residue, evaluated against
  163 alanine substitutions in 48 yeast proteins and 1,470 base-edited sites in 787 human
  proteins. Includes the offline source-to-cohort rebuild, the frozen estimator, and
  NUMBERS.md, which records every reported value and the claims that were retracted.
keywords:
  - phosphorylation
  - AlphaFold
  - yeast
  - human
  - mutational phenotype
  - structural bioinformatics
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: article
    title: "High-throughput functional characterization of protein phosphorylation sites in yeast"
    authors:
      - family-names: Vieitez
        given-names: Cristina
    doi: "10.1038/s41587-021-01051-x"
    year: 2022
  - type: article
    title: "Post-translational modification-centric base editor screens to assess phosphorylation site functionality in high throughput"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kennedy
        given-names: Philip H.
    doi: "10.1038/s41592-024-02256-z"
    year: 2024
